WEBVTT

00:00:00.261 --> 00:00:03.620
Haze, smoke, fog, rain, snow, low cloud, glare,

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:06.320
and low light reduce visual contrast and depth cues.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:10.120
They can affect the operator's view of the aircraft, surrounding airspace, terrain,

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.825
and obstacles even when the camera feed appears bright.

00:00:12.825 --> 00:00:16.350
Visual-line-of-sight requirements and operational awareness apply to the whole scene,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.760
not only an aircraft light.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.770
If the pilot cannot reliably judge position, orientation, flight path, or hazards,

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:23.800
the mission should not continue.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.050
Sensors have limits.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.315
Automatic exposure may brighten a scene while increasing noise or blur.

00:00:28.315 --> 00:00:30.778
Precipitation and wind can destabilize footage.

00:00:30.778 --> 00:00:34.880
Haze and smoke can remove fine detail or change apparent color and distance.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.222
Data quality should be part of go or no-go criteria.

00:00:37.222 --> 00:00:40.120
Define the detail and accuracy needed before flight.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.840
If conditions cannot produce evidence suitable for the decision,

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.050
taking the flight adds risk without mission value.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:48.680
A visible aircraft light does not prove that the surrounding route is visible.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:52.285
The operator must still recognize attitude, trajectory, terrain, obstacles,

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:54.675
and nearby airspace well enough for controlled flight.

00:00:54.675 --> 00:00:58.940
Review a sample when safe and watch for lens obstruction, focus loss, vibration,

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:02.720
motion blur, compression, low contrast, or inconsistent mapping overlap.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.245
Avoid interpreting detail that the sensor did not capture reliably.

00:01:06.245 --> 00:01:09.135
Document visibility, weather, lighting, wind, sensor settings,

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.320
and limitations for later analysis.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:14.860
A report should explain whether poor conditions could hide features or create apparent

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:15.360
changes.
